      },
      "message": "fix(pathkernel): Exit::new takes the material top and refuses a retract under it\n\nExit::new(lead_out, retract, top) and Exit::proved share check_retract: RAPID_IN_MATERIAL for a retract under the top, BAD_EXIT for a value that is not finite. The callers in the law suite and the converter tests pass the top of their fixtures. Pinned by no_silent_exit::the_exit_constructors_share_one_checked_path. The work of #4415.\n\nRefs #4407\nRefs #4383\nRefs #4415\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
